  "title": "Prayers for the Nights of Ramazan",
  "data": "## First Night Prayer\nFour units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) fifteen times.\n\n## Second Night Prayer\nFour units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Qadr](A101) twenty times.\n\n## Third Night Prayer\nTen units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) fifty times.\n\n## Fourth Night Prayer\nEight units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Qadr](A101) twenty times.\n\n## Fifth Night Prayer\nTwo units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) fifty times. After accomplishment, SWALAWAT is repeated one hundred times:\n\n## Sixth Night Prayer\nFour units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Mulk](A71) (No. 67).\n\n## Seventh Night Prayer\nFour units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Qadr](A101) thirteen times.\n\n## Eighth Night Prayer\nTwo units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) ten times. After accomplishment, SUBHANA ALLAH is repeated one thousand times:\n\n## Ninth Night Prayer\nSix units offered between the Maghrib and Isha’ obligatory Prayers with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) seven times. After accomplishment, SWALAWAT is repeated fifty times:\n\n## Tenth Night Prayer\nTwenty units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) thirty times.\n\n## Eleventh Night Prayer\nTwo units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Kawthar](A112) (No. 108) twenty times.\n\n## Twelfth Night Prayer\nEight units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Qadr](A101) thirty times.\n\n## Thirteenth Night Prayer\nFour units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) twenty-five times.\n\n## Fourteenth Night Prayer\nSix units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Zalzalah](A103) (No. 99) thirty times.\n\n## Fifteenth Night Prayer\nFour units; in the first two units, [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) is recited once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) repeated one hundred times. In the last two units, [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) is recited once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) repeated fifty times.\n\n## Sixteenth Night Prayer\nTwelve units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Takathur](A106) (No. 102) twelve times.\n\n## Seventeenth Night Prayer\nTwo units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and any selected Surah in the first unit and [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) one hundred times. After accomplishment, LA ILAHA ILLA ALLAH is repeated one hundred times:\n\n## Eighteenth Night Prayer\nFour units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Kawthar](A112) twenty-five times.\n\n## Nineteenth Night Prayer\nFifty units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Zalzalah](A103) (No. 99).\n\n## Twentieth to Twenty-Fourth Nights Prayer\nAt these nights, it is recommended to offer an eight unit prayer with any selected Surahs.\n\n## Twenty-Fifth Night Prayer\nEight units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) ten times.\n\n## Twenty-Sixth Night Prayer\nEight units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) one hundred times.\n\n## Twenty-Seventh Night Prayer\nFour units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Mulk](A71). If this is impossible, replace [Surah al-Mulk](A71) with repeating [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) twenty-five times.\n\n## Twenty-Eighth Night Prayer\nSix units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) one hundred times, [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) one hundred times, and [Surah al-Kawthar](A112) one hundred times. After accomplishment, SWALAWAT is repeated one hundred times:\n\nAccording to my own readings in the books of narrations, I found that the prayer of the twenty-eighth night of Ramadan consists of six units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once, [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) ten times, [Surah al-Kawthar](A112) ten times, and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) ten times. After accomplishment the same invocation is repeated one hundred times.\n\n## Twenty-Ninth Night Prayer\nTwo units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) twenty times.\n\n## Thirtieth Night Prayer\nTwelve units with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) twenty times. After accomplishment, SWALAWAT is repeated one hundred times:\n\nNote that each two units of all of these prayers should be separated by uttering the Taslim statement.",
  "merits": "In Zad al-Ma’ad, ‘Allamah al-Majlisi has referred to the prayers of Ramadan nights in the last chapter of the recommended rites of Ramadan. Hereby, I will refer to these prayers as briefly as mentioned in the book involved:"
